---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /ecosystem/
title: Ecosystem — Turborel
description: Use Turborel from Rust, where it's built in, or from JavaScript, Python, Go, Java, C#, C++, C, PHP and Ruby with the official ecosystem. Plus the CLI, Studio, Helm charts and drivers from the community.
crumbs: [{ label: "Turborel", url: "/" }, { label: "Ecosystem" }]
---
{#- Everything here comes from src/_data/ecosystem.js; community entries are
    added there by pull request. #}
{%- set latest = releases[0] %}
<div class="wrap layout single">
  <main id="content" class="sheet">
    <article class="doc ecosystem">
      <h1 class="page-title">Ecosystem</h1>
      <p class="lede">Drivers for your language, the tools that come with Turborel, ways to run it on Kubernetes, and projects from the community.</p>

      <h2>Built in</h2>
      <p><strong>{{ ecosystem.builtin.language }}.</strong> Turborel is written in Rust, and its Rust library ships with the server and the CLI in <a href="{{ ecosystem.builtin.url }}"><code>{{ ecosystem.builtin.repo }}</code></a>. Embed the database in your application, or connect to a <code>turboreld</code> server.</p>

      <h2>Official drivers</h2>
      <p>Maintained by the Turborel project, and released together with the server: a driver&rsquo;s version is the server version it was built for.{% if not latest %} There are no releases yet, so every driver follows its repo&rsquo;s main branch, alongside the server&rsquo;s.{% endif %}</p>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Language</th><th>Repository</th><th>Version</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- for d in ecosystem.official %}
          <tr><td>{{ d.language }}</td><td><a href="{{ d.url }}"><code>{{ d.repo }}</code></a></td><td>{% if latest %}{{ latest.version }}{% else %}alpha{% endif %}</td></tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h2>Tools</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table>
        <tbody>
          {%- for t in ecosystem.tools %}
          <tr><td><strong>{{ t.name }}</strong></td><td>{{ t.description }}</td><td><a href="{{ t.url }}"><code>{{ t.repo }}</code></a></td></tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h2>Kubernetes</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table>
        <tbody>
          {%- for k in ecosystem.kubernetes %}
          <tr><td><strong><a href="{{ k.url }}">{{ k.name }}</a></strong></td><td>{{ k.description }}{% if k.install %}<br><code>{{ k.install }}</code>{% endif %}</td><td><a href="https://github.com/{{ k.repo }}"><code>{{ k.repo }}</code></a></td></tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h2>From the community</h2>
      {%- if ecosystem.community.length %}
      <div class="table-wrap"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Language</th><th>Project</th><th>About</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- for c in ecosystem.community %}
          <tr><td>{{ c.language }}</td><td><a href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.name }}</a>{% if c.by %} by {{ c.by }}{% endif %}</td><td>{{ c.description }}</td></tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p>Community projects are listed as their authors describe them; the Turborel project doesn&rsquo;t maintain or review them.</p>
      {%- else %}
      <p class="none">None yet.</p>
      {%- endif %}
      <p>Wrote a driver or a tool? Add it to <a href="https://github.com/turborel/turborel.github.io/blob/main/src/_data/ecosystem.js"><code>src/_data/ecosystem.js</code></a> in the website&rsquo;s repository and open a pull request.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</div>
